# Wanderwine Farewell: "Return one or two target nonland permanents to their owners' hands. Then if you control a Merfolk, create a 1/1 white and blue Merfolk
# creature token for each permanent returned." The order matters: Bot1 returns its own Merfolk of the Pearl Trident, its only Merfolk, with Bot2's Raiders, so after
# the return it controls none and no token is made, though two permanents were returned.

[Bot1 Deck]
Merfolk of the Pearl Trident
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Wanderwine Farewell
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mons's Goblin Raiders
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Merfolk of the Pearl Trident.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Mons's Goblin Raiders.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: U)
Bot1.Hand.Wanderwine Farewell.Cast(Convoke: Ornithopter, Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Mons's Goblin Raiders; Bot1.Battlefield.Merfolk of the Pearl Trident)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand = Merfolk of the Pearl Trident; Island
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby
Bot2.Graveyard =
Bot1.Battlefield = Ornithopter; Ornithopter; Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet
